> 
> >From my perspective that makes code to look really ugly...
> If the static initialization is not possible, can we simply change the code to do memset() before first usage of the array?

I agree that the compact notation allowed by the gcc extension is nice, but unfortunately msvc does not implement it.

This subject has previously been addressed [1], and it was noted that, given the existing use of explicitly populated
fixed arrays within this file (such as zuc_test_auth_5670b), the proposed modification is considered acceptable.

[1] https://inbox.dpdk.org/dev/CAJFAV8wx0yZXctq90Q2b4PBoA6GVrpMgKQCudWgij==Lf4cDAw@mail.gmail.com/

